-- Two defects the qnfo-model-eval fold cleanup met, each with the reading that proves it, filed with a doer (code-task, code-anchor, code-probe) so neither stays prose:
--  1. UNBIND-VERIFY-RETRY-1: cf-ops-actions unbind-service reported ok=false although the binding was gone. Run 41966513551 (2026-11-05T04:14Z): the settings PATCH answered http 200 and the version it created (04:14:21Z) holds 69 bindings without
--     CH_QNFO_MODEL_EVAL, but the action's own after-read still showed 70 bindings (read-after-write lag of the settings endpoint), so it exited 1 and scripts/ci_watchdog.py filed GitHub issue 7694 ("a successful re-run closes this finding"); a re-run
--     after the redeclaration is refused by design, so the finding could never close by its own rule. The same single after-read sits in unbind_d1.
--  2. BINDING-INSTALL-FETCH-1: qnfo-ops installDeclaredBindings returns "no wrangler.toml" and the deploy still reports OK when the contents fetch fails once. canonical-deploy run 41966765971 (04:16:53Z, deployment_history 3339) read
--     "observability=none declared" and installed no binding; the identical dispatch three minutes later (3340, "observability=applied") installed CH_QNFO_MODEL_EVAL. A fold or a new binding silently does not arrive on one bad fetch.
-- Files are held by other sessions today (scripts/cf_ops_actions.py by C-ops-tools-F4, qnfo-ops/worker.js by C-ops-tools), so the doer is the code loop; this migration only files the work.
