 'QNFO.INFRA; charter pillar core; roadmap rows RM-TP-3-FOOTPRINT-TEARDOWN (128) and RM-TP-2-ONE-KERNEL (127); every fold of a worker with a probe binding goes through this action. Read 2026-11-05: run 41966513551 unbind-service qnfo-ops:CH_QNFO_MODEL_EVAL answered the settings PATCH with http 200 and no errors, the version Cloudflare created at 04:14:21Z holds 69 bindings without the binding, yet the action''s after-read (GET settings) returned 70 and the action exited 1 (ok false, bindings_before 70, bindings_after 70). ci-watchdog filed GitHub issue 7694 whose rule is "a successful re-run closes this finding"; after the binding is re-declared to the host (SERVICE-REPOINT-1) a re-run is refused by design, so the finding cannot close. Work in scripts/cf_ops_actions.py unbind_service (and the same single read in unbind_d1): after the PATCH re-read the settings up to 6 times with a 5 s pause until the binding is absent and the count is one lower; if the reads still disagree, read the newest script version (GET workers/scripts/<w>/versions, then versions/<id> resources.bindings) and trust it; report which read confirmed and how many tries it took in the RESULT_JSON (verified_by, tries). Test (scripts/cf_ops_delete_worker_test.py pattern, no network): a fake API whose settings read returns the old list for the first three reads, then the new one, gives ok true with tries 4; a PATCH that fails still gives ok false; a binding that is still present on the newest version gives ok false. Prediction: no unbind-service run reports ok false while the newest version lacks the binding (the watchdog action-result finding for unbind-service stops being filed). Closing marker: the change carries the text UNBIND-VERIFY-RETRY-1. Refs GitHub 7694.' || char(10) ||
